   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What was said and what is observed",
     "texto": [
      "**-다더니** links something said, expected or observed earlier with the situation that followed. It can confirm an impression or point out that reality was different: 온다 → **온다더니**; 좋다 → **좋다더니**; 학생이라 → **학생이라더니**.",
      "사람이 많다더니 정말 복잡하네요 = they said there would be a lot of people, and indeed it is crowded."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "It does not always imply a contradiction",
     "texto": [
      "The relation depends on the context: the result can match what was said or contrast with it. The subject of the first part can also be the speaker if it refers to an earlier observation.",
      "비가 온다더니 정말 비가 오네요 = they said it would rain, and indeed it is raining."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
